            "name": "model prediction",
            "datasetColumnName": "prediction",
            "type": "TEXT"
          }
        ],
        "structuredPromptPrefix": "Summarise this pending loan application for a loan officer in two or three plain sentences: the amount, length and purpose, the FICO range and debt-to-income ratio, and the model\u0027s default probability. Say clearly that the probability is a prediction that supports a person\u0027s decision and never recommend approving or declining. End with one thing the officer could check, phrased as a question.",
        "structuredPromptExamples": [
          {
            "inputs": [
              "69741",
              "6000",
              "36",
              "credit_card",
              "690-694",
              "0.1905",
              "0.6805",
              "1.0"
            ],
            "output": "Application 69741 asks for 6,000 US dollars over 36 months for a credit card payoff, with a FICO range of 690-694 and a debt-to-income ratio of 0.19. The model puts the default probability at 0.68, a prediction that supports the officer\u0027s decision rather than making it. The officer could ask whether the income documents support the monthly payment."
          },
